 <h2 style="margin-top:16px">We Do 2: Match the Source → What It's Genuinely Useful For</h2><p>Draw lines to match:</p><p>📜 Recruitment poster · 📒 Landlady's account book · ⛪ Baptism register · ✉️ Anonymous complaint · 📷 Works publicity photo · ⚖️ Coroner's inquest file</p><p>Dangers of the work, case by case · That grievance existed — voiced with risk · Family origins & settlement patterns · Rents, diets, overcrowding, arrears · The labour shortage & recruiters' lures · How the company wished to be seen</p></div><div id="print-scaffold-supported" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding – Supported</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Word Bank</h3><p>nature, origin, purpose, useful for, not for, because</p><h3>Frames</h3><p>"Its nature is…" | "It was made to…" | "Useful for ___ but not for ___"</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-standard" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding – Standard</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Utility Structure</h3><p><strong>Enquiry:</strong> named first. <strong>NOP:</strong> one line each. <strong>Yield:</strong> 'genuinely useful for…' <strong>Bar:</strong> 'but not for…' <strong>Partner:</strong> what a second source adds.</p></div></div><div id="print-scaffold-stretch" class="print-section"><h2>Scaffolding – Stretch</h2><div class="scaffold-print-box"><h3>Inversion frames</h3><p>"For an enquiry into ___, the poster outranks the census because ___" | "Purpose here is not a flaw but the evidence itself" | "The census, by nature, cannot witness ___"</p></div></div><div id="print-reference" class="print-section"><h2>&#128216; Reference Zone &mdash; keep this beside your work</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>No source is useful in the void. Name the enquiry first, or &ldquo;useful&rdquo; means nothing.</strong></p><h3>NOP &mdash; the archivist&rsquo;s triage</h3><table class="ko-table"><tr><th>Element</th><th>The question it asks</th><th>Why it changes the yield</th></tr><tr><td><strong>N &mdash; Nature</strong></td><td>What KIND of source is this?</td><td>Registers record. Posters persuade. The type has habits.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>O &mdash; Origin</strong></td><td>Who, when, where?</td><td>Proximity and stake &mdash; how close, and what did they gain?</td></tr><tr><td><strong>P &mdash; Purpose</strong></td><td>What job was it made to do?</td><td>The great predictor of what got selected in &mdash; and left out.</td></tr></table><h3>The utility verdict, in three moves</h3><p><strong>1. For the enquiry&hellip;</strong> name it. <strong>2. Genuinely useful for&hellip;</strong> the yield NOP actually licenses. <strong>3. But not for&hellip;</strong> the tempting misuse, barred out loud.</p><p><strong>Purpose is not always a flaw.</strong> A recruitment poster is weak evidence for real wages and superb evidence for the labour shortage &mdash; and for what recruiters thought would tempt a man. NOP does not dismiss a source. It re-aims it.</p></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-supported" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work – Supported</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>NOP Triage ×2</strong></p><p>Object 1 — N: ______ O: ______ P: ______</p><p>Best enquiry:</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>Object 2 — N: ______ O: ______ P: ______</p><p>Not useful for:</p><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-standard" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work – Standard</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>Full Utility Answer</strong></p><p>1) The enquiry:</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>2) NOP paragraph:</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><p>3) 'Genuinely useful for…':</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>4) 'But not for…':</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>5) Partner source + what it adds:</p><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-worksheet-stretch" class="print-section"><h2>Independent Work – Stretch</h2><div class="prevent-break"><p><strong>The Inversion Brief</strong></p><p>1) My chosen enquiry (built for the inversion):</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>2) Poster NOP vs census NOP (two lines each):</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><p>3) The inversion argued — purpose as evidence:</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class='print-line'></div><p>4) Partner-source postscript:</p><div class='print-line'></div></div></div><div id="print-exit" class="print-section"><div class="supported-content"><h2>Exit Ticket – Supported</h2><p>1) What do N, O, P stand for?</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>2) The account book is genuinely useful for…?</p><div class='print-line'></div><p>3) Complete: 'useful' always depends on the…</p><div class='print-line'></div><div class="print-section" id="print-lundy"><h2>Lundy Loop &mdash; this lesson</h2><p style="font-size:.95rem;color:#444">Space &rarr; Voice &rarr; Audience &rarr; Influence. The adult&rsquo;s first job is Space: regulate before you educate.</p><table class="ko-table"><tr><td style="width:22%;vertical-align:top"><strong>Space</strong></td><td>The Archive Box circulates table to table on YOUR schedule — negotiate handling order as a room.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:22%;vertical-align:top"><strong>Voice</strong></td><td>One 'not for' clause read aloud per pupil — barring the misuse is the week's spoken rite.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:22%;vertical-align:top"><strong>Audience</strong></td><td>Your utility verdicts are filed INTO the archive box for next year's LAUNCH class — you're writing to strangers.</td></tr><tr><td style="width:22%;vertical-align:top"><strong>Influence</strong></td><td>Select Week 4's century: which hundred years of Teesside change goes under the lens? House vote binds.</td></tr></table><p style="font-size:.95rem;margin:.5rem 0 0"><strong>Closing the loop:</strong> this one ends on paper &mdash; your own hand, or your words scribed by an adult. Saying it aloud starts the loop; writing it is what closes it. Pass is always allowed.</p><p style="font-siz